  "outcome": "escalate",
  "rationale": "The claim must be escalated because automated checks indicate it is unclear whether an exclusion applies due to open material facts from the claimant's account. Section [PLUS-6.2] governs this situation, mandating escalation when the available documents do not permit a definitive coverage determination.",
  "citations": [
    {
      "clause_id": "PLUS-6.2",
      "quote": "If the documents submitted do not allow the adjuster to determine whether an exclusion applies, because material facts are disputed, missing or open to more than one reasonable reading, the claim must be escalated for further investigation rather than approved or denied on the information available."
    }
  ]
}
